==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{q|obsolete}} {{l|en|systematick}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|LL.|systēmaticus}}, from {{der|en|grc-koi|συστηματικός}}, from {{suffix|grc|σύστημᾰ|t1=a composite; system|-ῐκός|pos2=adjective suffix|nocat=1}}. Cognate with {{cog|fr|systématique}} and {{cog|it|sistematico}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|systematic|''adj.'' and ''n.''|196668|noformat=1}}</ref> {{surf|en|system|-atic}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US|AU}} {{IPA|en|/ˌsɪs.təˈmæt.ɪk/}}
** {{a|US|AU}} {{IPA|en|[ˌsɪs.təˈmæɾ.ɪk]}}
*** {{audio|en|en-us-systematic.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ætɪk|s=4}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Carried out according to a [[planned]], [[ordered]] [[procedure]].
# {{lb|en|by extension}} [[methodical|Methodical]], [[regular]] and [[orderly]].
#: {{ant|en|chaotic|haphazard}}
# Treating an object as a [[system]] or [[coherent]] whole.
#: {{usex|en|the '''systematic''' study of religious beliefs}}
# {{lb|en|taxonomy}} Of or relating to [[taxonomic]] [[classification]].
# {{lb|en|chemistry}} Of, relating to, or in accordance with generally recognized [[convention]]s for the naming of [[chemical]]s.
# {{lb|en|archaic|or|academic}} Of, relating to, or being a [[system]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1878|title=A French Critic on Goethe|month=January|journal=w:The Quarterly Review|volume=145|number=289|page=145|pageurl=https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PYuxUL6ehs4C&pg=PA145|text=But the '''systematic''' judgment is altogether unprofitable. Its author has not really his eye upon the professed object of his criticism at all, but upon something else, which he wants to prove by means of that object. {{...}} As it is, all that he tells us is that he is no genuine critic, but a man with a system, an advocate.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1968|author=w:William J. Bouwsma|title=Venice and the Defense of Republican Liberty: Renaissance Values in the Age of Counter Reformation|page=219|text=And Paruta’s work also suggests that Venetians in the generation following the battle of Lepanto, although without altogether abandoning '''systematic''' views, were tending increasingly to look to history for their understanding of human affairs.}}

